  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 210</b></color></size>

    <b>The Iron Pillar of Delhi (replica)</b>

    <size=74%>c. 400 CE

    <i>Replica of a wrought-iron column, 7.2 m high</i>

    Replica made for this museum</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    This towering column was forged from wrought iron about 1,600 years ago and weighs some six tonnes. A Sanskrit inscription honours a king named Chandra, usually identified as the Gupta emperor Chandragupta II. Now in the Qutb complex in Delhi, the pillar has barely rusted, thanks to a thin protective film rich in phosphorus.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Replica made for this museum</color></size>'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
