  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 202</b></color></size>

    <b>Didarganj Yakshi</b>

    <size=74%>c. 3rd century BCE (date debated)

    <i>Polished Chunar sandstone, about 1.6 m high</i>

    Bihar Museum, Patna</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    This life-size female attendant holding a fly-whisk was found on the bank of the Ganga at Didarganj, Patna, in 1917. Its mirror-like polish is typical of Mauryan stone carving, though some scholars date it later. Yakshis were nature spirits associated with fertility and abundance.</size>'
