  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 201</b></color></size>

    <b>Lion Capital of Ashoka</b>

    <size=74%>c. 250 BCE

    <i>Polished Chunar sandstone, 2.15 m high</i>

    Sarnath Museum, Uttar Pradesh</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    Four lions stand back to back on a drum carved with a horse, a bull, an elephant and a lion separated by wheels, above an inverted lotus. The capital crowned a pillar Ashoka set up where the Buddha gave his first sermon. Adopted as India''s national emblem in 1950, its wheel also appears on the national flag.</size>'
